  |<#FFF4CC>| <<Week 7>> addition |
endlegend
@enduml

@startuml seq-8-event-cancellation
title Seq 8 — Organiser asks to cancel an event; Coordinator carries it out (SG2-67, SG2-56)\nas of main 4881413 (3 Nov 2026)
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFF4CC
actor "Event Organiser" as ORG
actor "Assigned Coordinator" as EC
actor "Registered Attendee" as ATT
participant "Web App" as WEB
participant "API\ncancellationHandlers" as API
database "Supabase Postgres" as DB

== Organiser asks (SG2-67 AC1) ==
ORG -> WEB : cancel event, with a reason (up to 500 characters)
WEB -> API : POST /api/event-requests/:eventId/cancellation-request {reason}\n[event_request.cancellation.request]
API -> DB : rpc request_event_cancellation(p_event_id, p_reason) (caller JWT)
DB -> DB : acting role = event_organiser; lock the event row; creator of the event (else 'missing');\nstatus draft / completed / cancelled / rejected -> 'closed'; already asked -> 'requested'
DB -> DB : cancellation_requested_at/by/reason on the event; history (cancellation_request);\nnotify the assigned Coordinator (cancellation_requested)
DB --> API : {outcome:'ok', coordinator_notified}
API --> WEB : 200
note right of DB : The status is unchanged until the Coordinator acts.

== Coordinator carries it out (SG2-67 AC1-AC5) ==
EC -> WEB : cancel the event (action hidden once the event is closed, #124)
WEB -> API : PATCH /api/event-requests/:eventId/cancel [event_request.cancel]
API -> DB : rpc cancel_event(p_event_id) (caller JWT)
DB -> DB : acting role = event_coordinator; lock venues, bookings, then the event;\nnot the assigned coordinator -> 'missing'; completed / cancelled / rejected -> 'closed';\nno cancellation request -> 'not_requested'
DB -> DB : release every held/confirmed venue booking that has not ended (its approved request -> cancelled);\nrelease tentative holds (their requests -> cancelled); cancel other pending venue and equipment requests
DB -> DB : events.status -> cancelled (cancelled_at/by, venue_booking_id cleared); history
DB -> DB : trigger release_cancelled_event_equipment (SG2-56): reservations released, one history entry each
DB -> DB : notify each registered attendee once and the Organiser (event_cancelled)
DB -> ATT : notification 'event_cancelled' with the reason
DB --> API : {outcome:'ok', status:'cancelled', bookings_released, attendees_notified}
API --> WEB : 200
note right of DB : keep_cancelled_events_cancelled refuses any later status change (AC5).\nWithdrawal, registration, change requests and planning edits are refused on a cancelled event.

